<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baz Bahadur Chand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1638–1678</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baz-bahadur">Baz Bahadur</a> Chand was a raja of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chand-dynasty">Chand dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumaon">Kumaon</a> in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a> and a contemporary of the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a>. He extended the kingdom northwards to the Tibetan border and campaigned against neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garhwal">Garhwal</a>. He is credited with building temples, including the Bhimeshwar temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhimtal">Bhimtal</a>, and strengthened Kumaon's links with the Mughal court.</p></div>
